  "solution": {
    "text": "In a given mixture, the ionization of two acids can be written as : Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></math> be degree of ionization at same concentration.<br /><math><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⇌</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></mrow></munder><munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math><br /><math><munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⇌</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</